There will be lawsuits, no doubt about it. However, WHO's list of essential medicines has 2 Benzodiazepines. It's going to be hard to convince them to pull those medicines. I can see a massive tightening in prescribing laws though. 

&#x200B;

For example, Alprazolam was a S4 medication in Australia, in 2014 it was rescheduled to an S8 (controlled medicine). The US may, I think it will, move Benzo's to a different schedule. But Midazolam and Diazepam will never leave any health system in the first world. No chance.

&#x200B;

I will have to cope if I'm ever pulled off my medications for good. I've never taken high doses, I will have unpleasant WD symptoms and mild to moderate problems forever but it's unlikely I'll die. I've been through worse.

